/* The brand art, as vector.
 *
 * Traced from the artwork supplied for the brand — the full-size English and
 * Arabic lockups — rather than from the small PNGs the app used to ship. Those
 * were 354px across at their largest, so at the size the sign-in page draws
 * the logo on a dense phone screen they were already below one-to-one: asking
 * for a bigger logo could only ask for a blurrier one. As vector it is sharp
 * at any size, and small enough to live in the bundle, so it is simply there
 * on first paint with nothing to fetch and nothing to reflow.
 *
 * The mark comes from the Arabic lockup, where nothing overlaps it — in the
 * English one the ascender of the "l" rises alongside the mark, and no clean
 * cut separates them. Both files carry the same drawing.
 *
 * The supplied artwork sits on black, so the silhouettes are lifted by
 * brightness and blurred a touch before tracing: they come from photographs,
 * and without that potrace faithfully reproduces the compression noise along
 * every edge.
 *
 * The mark keeps its gradient, sampled across its width from the supplied
 * file. The lettering is filled with currentColor, so it takes the colour of
 * wherever it sits rather than being locked to one white. */

